 "text": "Auditor\nSkip to main content\n10/18/2026 54° Clear\nSelect Language ​ ▼\nEnglish\nEnglish\nAfrikaans\nAlbanian\nArabic\nArmenian\nAzerbaijani\nBasque\nBelarusian\nBengali\nBosnian\nBulgarian\nCatalan\nCebuano\nChinese (Simplified)\nChinese (Traditional)\nCroatian\nCzech\nDanish\nDutch\nEsperanto\nEstonian\nFilipino\nFinnish\nFrench\nGalician\nGeorgian\nGerman\nGreek\nGujarati\nHaitian Creole\nHausa\nHebrew\nHindi\nHmong\nHungarian\nIcelandic\nIgbo\nIndonesian\nIrish\nItalian\nJapanese\nJavanese\nKannada\nKhmer\nKorean\nLao\nLatin\nLatvian\nLithuanian\nMacedonian\nMalay\nMaltese\nMaori\nMarathi\nMongolian\nNepali\nNorwegian\nPersian\nPolish\nPortuguese\nPunjabi\nRomanian\nRussian\nSerbian\nSlovak\nSlovenian\nSomali\nSpanish\nSwahili\nSwedish\nTamil\nTelugu\nThai\nTurkish\nUkrainian\nUrdu\nVietnamese\nWelsh\nYiddish\nYoruba\nZulu\n(515) 851-0202\nHome\nNews\nDepartments\nServices\nI Want to..\nHome\nNews\nDepartments\nAssessor\nAttorney\nAuditor\nBoard of Supervisors\nConservation\nEconomic Development\nEmergency Management\nEngineer/Secondary Roads\nEnvironmental Health\nPlanning & Zoning\nPublic Health\nRecorder\nSheriff\nTreasurer\nVeterans Affairs\nServices\nClerk of Court\nEmergency Financial Services\nPublic Transit\nWright County Charitable Foundation\nWright County Trails System\nTownship Trustees\nI Want To...\nAbsentee Vote\nApply for Courthouse Ground Use\nApply for a Marriage License\nDo a Property Search\nGet Copy of a Birth Certificate\nMove to Wright County\nPay Property Taxes / Vehicle Registration\nPetition for Drainage Repair\nRegister for Code Red\nRegister to Vote\nRenew my Driver's License\nEconomic Development\nEmployment Opportunities\nCounty Staff Listing\nslide 1 of 1\nAuditor\nSub Menu\nAuditor\nContact Us\nElections\nDrainage\nInteractive Drainage Map - Instructions\nUpcoming Drainage Activity & Meetings\nActive Petition for Repair\nDrainage District Petition for Repair Application\nOpen Repair & Improvement Projects\nDrainage District Historical Minutes\nDrainage Assessments\nDrainage District Engineer Maps\nElectronic Mail Request Form\nDrainage Open Ditch Videos\nDrainage Township Maps\nDrainage Resolutions\nDrainage Applications\nDrainage District Brush & Weed Control\nBudget Central\nClerk to the Board of Supervisors\nOther Duties of the Auditor\nTownship Trustees\nWoolstock Cemetery\nFireworks Permit Application\nReal Estate Information\nGIS Map Link - Wright County\nInteractive Transfer Books\nInteractive Survey Books\nInteractive Transfer Books - Instructions\nInteractive Survey Books - Instructions\nCounty Railroads\nMaps\nAnnual Audit Reports\nAnnual Financial Reports - Cash Basis\nBudget Reports\nHome\nDepartments\nAuditor\nAbout the Office of the Auditor\nThe office of the County Auditor was created in 1870 as part of a revamping of county government. The duties of the office covered areas that had previously been given to the County Judge in 1851, in the first Code of Iowa, and then to the Clerk of Court in 1861, with the formation of the Board of Supervisors. The State Legislature added the duties of Commissioner of Elections in the early 1970’s. The County Auditor is an elected position, with a term of four years.\nThe Institute of Public Affairs has labeled the Auditor’s Office as the “Hub of County Government”. The Auditors and their staff are always available to help with your questions and invite you to visit their offices anytime.\nThe following information has been prepared by the Iowa State Association of County Auditors for the purpose of acquainting you with the duties and responsibilities of your County Auditor. No attempt has been made to cover all the functions of this office. We hope you use this as a reference and an educational guide for information about the County Auditor.\nThe Auditor may perform a variety of duties depending on the size of the county and are described in the links on the right.\nBack to Top\nShare this page\nShare this page\n-->\nClose\nResources\nAmerica's SBDC Iowa\nHistory\nHome Base Iowa\nPay Property Taxes\nPhoto Credits\nRenew Vehicle Registration\nHelpful Links\nBoard of Supervisors\nCode Red\nCompensation Board\nElections\nReal Estate Transfer Calculator\nWright County Boards and Commissions\nContact us\nWright County Courthouse\n115 North Main Street\nClarion, Iowa 50525\n(515) 851-0202\nMonday - Friday\n8 a.m. - 4 p.m.\n© Wright County, lowa, All Rights Reserved. |\nSite Login\nPowered by revize . The Government Website Experts\nOriginal text\nRate this translation\nYour feedback will be used to help improve Google Translate\nClose Read More",
